{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# Bounded disk-ceiling architecture for the Gerrit host\n\n## Provenance / approved intent\nDiscovered from `cyclopean-bloodshot-hoatzin` (`3276-2f81-8c75-4ddd`), the 2026-09-02 root-volume outage that took Gerrit offline for ~5h. Defect 2 from that incident (disk alarms self-cleared when metrics stopped because `treat_missing_data=notBreaching`) stays on that bug and was fixed/landed/applied live. This epic is Defect 1: root-volume consumers grow without a bounded ceiling.\n\nOperator-approved design — firm standing intent, do not re-litigate:\n\n1. **Option A: per-accumulator HARD SIZE CAPS via native GC/retention.** Each disk consumer gets a hard upper bound enforced by its own native garbage-collection or retention mechanism. Consumers to cap: Docker overlay2/image layers + build cache (BuildKit/Docker GC policy with `maxUsedSpace` / `--keep-storage` style limits), `/var/tmp` (tmpfiles cleanup plus a real size/quota mechanism where required), journald (`SystemMaxUse`), and writable container layers (runtime storage quota where supportable, or bounded periodic reaping of exited containers). **Hard operator constraint:** every capped generator must have its own CloudWatch alarm at/near its cap, so capacity visibility names the saturated generator rather than only saying \"root disk high\".\n2. **Option C: separate EBS volume for code-review scratch.** Gate scratch/clones/snapshots currently share root via system temp (e.g. `/tmp/rebar-gate-snapshots`). Move this workload to a dedicated, independently sized/quota'd gp3 EBS volume mounted at a documented path, and configure gate temp/snapshot code so review work can never fill the OS/root disk.\n3. **Sibling carried from cyclopean AC5:** fold in `scowlful-bovine-dragonfly` (`3e92-b7f4-dede-4c17`), the `/var/gerrit` data-volume prevention/runbook task, by linking it into this epic rather than duplicating it.\n\nThe root volume was grown 30→60 GiB during recovery and should stay 60 GiB, but that is headroom only, not the fix: an unbounded generator can fill 60 GiB as readily as 30 GiB.\n\n## Research grounding\n- Current Terraform owns a single EC2 host plus `/var/gerrit` data EBS volume: `infra/terraform/main.tf:27-35`, `:42-64`, `:83-87`; size variables are in `infra/terraform/variables.tf:13-23`.\n- `infra/terraform/user_data.sh:20-70` is the existing attach/mount pattern: resolve Nitro NVMe device by EBS volume id, format idempotently, mount by UUID in `/etc/fstab`.\n- `infra/scripts/compose-up.sh:21-31` and `:82-99` create Docker bind volumes under `/var/gerrit/site`; current review-bot compose has no tmp/scratch mount and notes `REBAR_GATE_TMPDIR` is unset (`infra/compose/docker-compose.yml:233-245`).\n- Snapshot store and clone locations: `src/rebar/_snapshot/repo_snapshot.py:149-163` uses `REBAR_GATE_TMPDIR` else `tempfile.gettempdir()` and creates `rebar-gate-snapshots`; `src/rebar/review_bot/voter.py:381` clones into `tempfile.TemporaryDirectory(prefix=\"reviewbot-\")`; `src/rebar/review_bot/low_disk.py:69` checks free space on `tempfile.gettempdir()`.\n- Observability/alarm seams: `infra/scripts/observability.sh:72-90` publishes current data/root disk metrics; root alarm is `infra/terraform/monitoring_autodeploy.tf:207-239`; data alarm is `infra/terraform/monitoring.tf:217-244`.\n- Existing reactive reclaimers are in `infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh:132-140`, `:367-384`, and `:410-445`; runbook coverage is `infra/runbooks/review-bot-ops.md:494-606` and provisioning order is `infra/runbooks/provision-restore.md:98-138`.\n- Prior incident tickets found: `resting-feudalist-screamer` (`2731`), `masonic-abeyant-stagbeetle` (`3a52`), `besotted-witty-murrelet` (`e4f3`), `preodorous-temporary-piglet` (`3cef`), current `cyclopean-bloodshot-hoatzin` (`3276`), plus data-volume sibling `wakeful-ordinary-chicken` (`5a05`).\n\n## ADR draft location\nThe full ADR draft is captured in child story S0, to keep this epic under the 8,000-character plan-review admission cap. The implementation story should create `docs/adr/0110-gerrit-disk-ceiling-architecture.md` plus `docs/adr/.numbers/0110`, matching `docs/adr/README.md` and recent ADR format. Related accepted ADRs to cite: ADR 0005 (snapshot cache/janitor), ADR 0012 (AWS IaC foundations), ADR 0077/0069 (low-disk review behavior), ADR 0104 (dedicated MCP ticket-store volume precedent). No ADR file is created by this scaffold-only work.\n\n## Epic acceptance criteria\n- [ ] ADR 0110 is finalized and landed in `docs/adr/` with number marker and index update if required by repo convention.\n- [ ] Dedicated gate-scratch EBS volume exists, is mounted at a documented path, is used by gate snapshots and review clone tempdirs, and has its own disk alarm.\n- [ ] Each named root accumulator has an enforced cap and its own CloudWatch alarm at/near cap.\n- [ ] Existing root/data disk alarms remain present; the cyclopean missing-data fix is not regressed.\n- [ ] `scowlful-bovine-dragonfly` is resolved or remains a blocking dependency for epic close.\n- [ ] Runbooks document steady-state ceilings, per-generator alarms, and emergency remediation.\n- [ ] Portability criterion: implementation is Terraform + host Docker/systemd config + host metrics, with local/scripted validation; it does not depend on any single CI provider trigger.","priority":1}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788374907974680084,"uuid":"8f290556-ba3b-4fb8-ba8b-f7b4c30ee021"}